                <pb facs="0597" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115Ev2/4</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 22, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 24, 9.30 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1659. Consul General, Bremerhaven, reports steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Evelyn</hi> ran on two mines 19th, 4 a. m., near Isle Borkum, sank seven
                    hours later. Only two boats manned: Captain Smith, thirteen men, Dutch pilot in
                    one First Officer Swenson, thirteen men in other. First boat said to have been
                    rescued 10 o’clock Saturday morning, but present where-abouts yet unknown.
                    Latter boat picked up by German scoutship <hi rendition="#italic">Mars</hi> 4
                    o’clock Saturday afternoon; taken to Heligoland. Thirteen men brought to
                    Bremerhaven, put in sailors’ home. Spanish stoker, Hans Ilaro, frozen and buried
                    at sea; appears to be only death. Other survivors expected to-morrow. Those in
                    Bremerhaven out of danger.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
